--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
This file is the NOTICE of the Rust agent's image
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The repository's NOTICE describes the Java images: the jars and the Alpine base
they run on. This one describes the Rust agent's image, which holds a single
statically linked program, /vectispire-agent, on an empty base (`scratch`):
no operating-system package, no shell, nothing else.

A static binary carries none of its dependencies' licence texts, where a jar
carries them in META-INF. They are in the image beside this file:

  /app/THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES   every Rust crate linked into the binary, with the
                              licence it declares and every licence file it
                              ships, and the C libraries compiled into it.
                              Generated from Cargo.lock by
                              vectispire-rust/security/third-party-licences.py,
                              which also checks that this file names every
                              licence listed there.
  /app/RUST-STD-COPYRIGHT.html
                              the Rust standard library's own notices, as the
                              pinned toolchain ships them — musl libc and LLVM's
                              libunwind among them, both linked statically.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Licences of the components linked into the binary
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The crates are permissively licensed; most offer a choice ("MIT OR
Apache-2.0"), and the list above carries every text they ship, so no choice
is made on anyone's behalf. The licences found in the graph:

  Apache-2.0 (also Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception), MIT, BSD-3-Clause, ISC,
  Zlib, BSL-1.0 and Unlicense (each offered beside MIT or Apache-2.0)

  Unicode-3.0           the ICU4X crates (URL and IDNA handling): the Unicode
                        data they embed
  CDLA-Permissive-2.0   webpki-roots: Mozilla's list of certificate
                        authorities, compiled in as the agent's default trust

Apache-2.0 asks that a component's own NOTICE be passed on: the ones the crates
ship are in /app/THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES with the rest.

C libraries compiled from source and linked in, under their own licences,
whatever the licence of the crate that builds them:

  libgit2   GPL-2.0 with the libgit2 linking exception (git2 / libgit2-sys).
            The exception permits linking it, unmodified, into a program under
            any licence and distributing the result; libgit2's source is
            https://github.com/libgit2/libgit2 at the version the crate names
            (1.9.7). Its COPYING, with the notices of the code it bundles, is
            in /app/THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.
  libssh2   BSD-3-Clause (libssh2-sys)
  zlib      Zlib (libz-sys)
  OpenSSL   Apache-2.0 (openssl-src, libssh2's cryptography)

The scanners the agent runs are separate images, pulled from their publishers
at run time; it bundles none of them. The repository's NOTICE lists them.
